       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is double the 3200 mg/day maximum in the prescribing labeling. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual 800 mg per-dose maximum. For a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function, this is likely a dosing error.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO QID** (1600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO QID** (2400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO TID** (2400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO QID** (3200 mg/day, the labeled maximum, which is usually the upper limit)\n- Or 1600 mg PO TID, if you intentionally want 4800 mg/day (this exceeds the labeled maximum, so please confirm)\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it. Given the GI and renal risks of NSAIDs at high doses, please also confirm the indication and duration."
